virglrenderer: Vulkan windows without a copy on macOS (IOSurface window buffers)

What: with OMACVM_VK_WINDOWS=iosurface (OmacVM.app's vkWindowsNoCopy) and
KosmicKrisp, vkr makes the buffer Mesa's WSI exports for a Vulkan window (the
PRIME blit target: transfer target only, exported as a dma-buf, a dedicated
allocation) out of an IOSurface of 16 KiB rows (4096 BGRA texels a row),
imported into the driver as host memory (VK_EXT_external_memory_host; the buffer
is created with that handle type). The blob is a new resource type,
VIRGL_RESOURCE_IOSURFACE (mapped as the IOSurface's own pages). When Hyprland
imports it (PIPE_RESOURCE_SET_TYPE without EGL), vrend binds the IOSurface as a
GL_TEXTURE_RECTANGLE and, when a draw samples the window, the blitter's own GL
context re-strides it into the window's 2D texture with a small shader: 4-byte
BGRA- or RGBA-ordered pixels, or 8-byte half-float pixels taken apart bit by
bit (vkcube's format on Hyprland). Ordering: Venus finished the buffer before
the guest handed it over; the re-stride is fenced into the guest's context
(glFenceSync/glWaitSync), so the command buffer's own fence covers the read,
and the guest writes the buffer again only after that fence (its implicit fence
on the dma-buf). No CPU copy, no CPU wait.
Why: the CPU copy (virgl-set-type-without-egl.patch) ran on QEMU's main loop,
with the BQL, on every compositor frame that showed a Vulkan window: 2.5 ms for
a 1816x870 FP16 window, 1.8-2.3 ms full screen at 3680x1840 (Mac mini M4), up
to 5.6 ms at 4K when the GPU is busy. Re-stride: 0.3-0.4 ms of QEMU's time.
Fails closed: another driver (MoltenVK), no host memory import, any other
format, a layout outside the IOSurface, or a failed bind: the CPU copy from the
same pages (or, when the IOSurface itself cannot be made, the Metal heap path),
logged once. Every guest size is checked before Metal, IOSurface or CGL see it
(vrend_iosurface_layout_ok). The IOSurface's pages outlive the Vulkan memory
until every queue of the device passed the guest's vkFreeMemory (an empty
submission per queue holds a reference), so the GPU never touches freed pages.
Limits: such a buffer cannot be imported into another Venus context (a Vulkan
compositor in the guest: VK_ERROR_INVALID_EXTERNAL_HANDLE); OFF by default.
Upstream: not sent (macOS only; upstream's Metal path needs EGL on ANGLE).
Test: Tests/virgl/test-vulkan-window-restride.c (build time: the real shader and
draw on the Mac's OpenGL, bit-exact for all three layouts with offsets and
strides that cross rows; the layout check's boundaries and overflows); the
Vulkan validation layer on the host harness (work/vulkan-zc/kit/zchost.m: no
errors with the host allocation handle type); VM: vkcube, vkmark windowed and
full screen, Xwayland, resize, two windows, gpuOffMainLoop, MoltenVK (copy),
30-minute soak (track notes vulkan-zero-copy.md section 7, ADR 0047).

